quran[30]{c,v,t}:
  74,18,"Indeed, he reflected and plotted."
  74,19,So may he perish! How he plotted!
  74,20,"Again, may he perish! How he plotted!"
  74,21,Then he looked (into his scheme again).
  74,22,Then he frowned and twisted his face.
  74,23,"Then he turned his back and showed arrogance,"
  74,24,and said: ‘This (Qur’an) is nothing but magic transmitted (from the ancients).
  74,25,This is nothing but the word of a man.’
  74,26,I shall soon burn him in Saqar (the Fire of Hell).*
  74,27,What will make you realise what Saqar is?
  74,28,It (is the Hellfire which) does not let anyone live nor leave to die.
  74,29,It burns and blackens the skin.
  74,30,There are nineteen (guards) over it.
  74,31,"And We have appointed none but angels as the wardens of the Fire. And We have not made their number but as a test for the disbelievers, so that the People of the Book be reassured, and the believers may increase in (their) faith. And those given the Book may not doubt, and the believers as well. And those in whose hearts is a disease (of hypocrisy) may say, and the disbelievers as well: ‘What does Allah intend by this example?’ In this way, Allah leaves whomever He wills to stray and guides whomever He pleases. And none knows (the number of) the forces of your Lord except Him. And this (description of Hell) is only a reminder for all humans."
  74,32,"No, indeed! By the moon!"
  74,33,"By the night, when it retreats!"
  74,34,"By the morning, when it brightens!"
  74,35,"Indeed! It (i.e. Hell) is one of the greatest (calamities),"
  74,36,"a warner to all humans,"
  74,37,for those of you who wish to take the lead or those who linger behind (trapped in evil).
  74,38,"Every soul is held in pledge for what it has earned,"
  74,39,except the People of the Right Hand.
  74,40,"(They will be) in Gardens, asking one another,"
  74,41,about the evildoers:
  74,42,‘What has led you into Saqar (i.e. the Hellfire)?’
  74,43,"They will answer: ‘We were not among those who prayed,"
  74,44,nor did we feed the poor.
  74,45,"We used to gossip with the gossipers (in mocking the believers),"
  74,46,"and we used to deny the Day of Judgement,"
  74,47,until the Certain End came upon us.’
